==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|vinden|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|findan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|finþaną|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|pent-||to go, pass; path, bridge|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Low German {{term|finden|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|vinden|lang=nl}}, English {{term|find|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|finde|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈfɪndn̩]|[ˈfɪndən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-finden.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|De-at-finden.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=3|findet|fand|gefunden|past subjunctive=fände}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=de}} to [[find]]; to [[discover]]
# {{context|transitive|with a noun phrase and a predicate adjective|lang=de}} to [[think]] that (something) is (a certain way); to [[consider]] (something) to be (a certain way); to [[find]]
# {{context|intransitive|lang=de}} to find one’s way

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj-strong|find|fand|gefunden|h|e||fänd|a}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l/de|abfinden}}
* {{l/de|einfinden}}
* {{l/de|erfinden}}
* {{l/de|herausfinden}}

